[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDGE-ARC-SCOPE
TITLE: Candidate status and composition
STATUS: proposed
KIND: design scope
SOURCE: EDG-REQ-0001 through EDG-REQ-0033
STATEMENT: >>>
This is a proposed architecture, not a new requirement set or approval to migrate code. Requirement authority remains edge.sdoc; all its 33 entries are proposed.
Design input: allocation schema edge-allocation-draft/v1, SHA256 A8B95CE1AF2C2DC2E74DB432A0F54D8DCFE0B7B28ED1AFF2E8637AB598A6646E.
Requirement bytes SHA256 22D995CB07DEFF45D31868669A5B6B851EB8CD4696A0675C497D9A4F7D86C028 at parent commit e4b598c8ae76163532ff052f3d3b94de00c6e7b1.
Eleven logical modules are not eleven deployments or mandatory packages. Existing run entry points compose PAR -> INF -> DEC and submit artifacts to EVA and REC. The entry point passes image/task/config, never labels, to runtime components. EVA alone receives references for offline scoring/calibration.
RPL is the replay composition root: it loads fixed traces, tasks, recorded outputs, profiles and configuration; assembles each DecisionInputs at current event time; calls POL; applies fallback and logs all requests. IF-11 denotes profile provenance, not a live MEA-to-POL call; profiles always enter POL through RPL's IF-13. IF-19's DAT role is artifact validation/packaging, not recomputing findings. Runtime and artifact cycles are not source-import dependencies.
No B0 module dependency, hardware inference, raw dataset endpoint access or test-set use is authorised here. All integration checks below are planned, not run. v2 instructions are not an evaluation source for this architecture; do not read or score them. A future independent v3 or a format-only downgrade is a separate decision.
S2 produces a reviewable draft; S3 requires Owner approval and explicit decisions on open items. No threshold defaults, code migration, PR merge or freeze tags.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDGE-ARC-TYPES
TITLE: Shared signature notation and field types
STATUS: proposed
KIND: interface type dictionary
SOURCE: EDG-REQ-0001 0002 0003 0008 0018 0021
STATEMENT: >>>
Signatures are Python typing notation for design, not executable declarations. Fields below are exhaustive logical records, with Optional denoted by | None. Named types are immutable; collections are tuples; no hidden globals. Tagged unions retain distinct failure, invalid and abstain states. Identifiers are nonempty str; hashes are 64 hexadecimal characters; bool is never accepted as int. Floats are finite. Unit-bearing suffixes are normative for this draft; no numerical performance limits are set.
ArtifactRef(path: str, sha256: str, format_version: str): path is a caller-authorised local artifact, no network fetch, hash is verified before use. Path containment and symlink policy are checked by composition.
SchemaRef(id: str, sha256: str, vocabulary: tuple[str, ...]): nonempty versioned closed sets.
ValidationResult(valid: bool, errors: tuple[str, ...]): valid iff errors empty; no silent coercion.
Failure(request_id: str, kind: Literal['reject','execution_error','timeout','unsupported'], reason: str, raw_ref: ArtifactRef | None): infrastructure failure is not an abstention.
TaskRecord(target_element: str, location_tag: str, defect_classes: tuple[str, ...], required_views: tuple[str, ...]): target/location/views are validated against pinned task schema; defects/views nonempty and unique. Mapping to dataset classes is explicit, never string similarity.
ParseArtifact(instruction_id: str, status: Literal['task','rejected'], task: TaskRecord | None, reason: str | None, raw_ref: ArtifactRef, parser_config: ArtifactRef, schema: SchemaRef): task iff status task; rejection has reason and no task.
TaskEnvelope(request_id: str, instruction_id: str, task: TaskRecord, task_sha256: str, schema: SchemaRef).
ImageMeta(image_id: str, width_px: int, height_px: int, capture: CaptureStamp): positive dimensions, top-left origin.
ImageRef(artifact: ArtifactRef, meta: ImageMeta, split_id: str, source_inventory: ArtifactRef).
ImageInput(meta: ImageMeta, pixels: bytes, content_sha256: str, format: str): decoded bytes interpretation declared by format; no annotation fields.
TransformMeta(source: ImageMeta, processed_width_px: int, processed_height_px: int, transform_id: str, forward_parameters: tuple[float, ...], inverse_parameters: tuple[float, ...]): positive dimensions, finite and invertible for declared crop/resize convention; no implicit clipping. Exact pixel-edge convention must be in config before evaluation.
Box(x_min_px: float, y_min_px: float, x_max_px: float, y_max_px: float): source-pixel edge coordinates, 0 <= xmin < xmax <= width and 0 <= ymin < ymax <= height. Bounds derive from image dimensions, not acceptance thresholds.
Finding(class_id: str, box: Box, confidence: float): closed dataset-version class, confidence in [0,1] per 0018.
FindingRecord(status: Literal['findings','no_finding','abstain','invalid'], entries: tuple[Finding, ...], reason: str | None): findings has nonempty entries; other statuses empty entries; abstain/invalid require reason. no_finding is a valid claim, not automatically correct.
FindingArtifact(request_id: str, image: ImageMeta, record: FindingRecord | None, failure: Failure | None, raw_ref: ArtifactRef, decode_config: ArtifactRef): exactly one of record/failure. Never includes reference labels.
DecodeConfig(artifact: ArtifactRef, vocabulary: SchemaRef, transform_policy: str, confidence_rule: str, abstention_rule: str, parameter_values: tuple[tuple[str, float | str], ...], calibration_manifest: ArtifactRef, frozen: bool): parameter values require Owner resolution then calibration-only determination; no runnable default in this draft.
InferenceRequest(task: TaskEnvelope, image: ImageInput, model: ModelConfig, decode_contract: ArtifactRef).
ModelConfig(model_id: str, revision: str, precision: str, libraries: tuple[tuple[str,str], ...], device_id: str, prompt: ArtifactRef, processor: ArtifactRef, generation: ArtifactRef): pinned identifiers, no selection after test.
RawArtifact(request_id: str, raw_ref: ArtifactRef, model: ModelConfig, transform: TransformMeta, runtime_signals: tuple[tuple[str,float], ...], events: tuple[MeasurementEvent, ...], failure: Failure | None): signals are actually available outputs, not reference correctness.
DeviceRequest(device_id: str, precision: str).
DeviceInfo(device_id: str, host_id: str, host_type: Literal['development-host'], supported_precision: tuple[str,...], available_memory_mib: float | None, libraries: tuple[tuple[str,str], ...]): memory nonnegative or unknown.
ProbeRequest(device_id: str, tool_id: str, channels: tuple[str,...]).
HostSample(host_id: str, device_id: str, host_type: Literal['development-host'], stamp: HostStamp, tool_id: str, power_w: float | None, memory_mib: float | None, clock_mode: str | None): available readings nonnegative, absence explicit. No claim of instantaneous peak from polling.
DeviceProfile(profile_id: str, location: Literal['onboard','edge','cloud','split'], source: Literal['measured','declared','modelled'], artifact: ArtifactRef, latency_s: float, energy_j: float | None, memory_mib: float | None, measurement_boundary: str): nonnegative costs; location is a hypothetical replay placement, not host identity; source preserved per field in artifact.
StampedProfile(profile: DeviceProfile, available_at: ReplayStamp).
Placement = Literal['onboard','edge','cloud','split'].
StampedValue(value: float | str | bool, stamp: ReplayStamp, source: ArtifactRef): generic scalar, units defined by named field.
DecisionInputs(request_id: str, task: TaskRecord, now: ReplayStamp, capture: CaptureStamp, profiles: tuple[StampedProfile,...], link: LinkSample, time_budget_ticks: int, energy_budget_j: float | None, input_freshness_ticks: int, result_freshness_ticks: int, completed_quality: QualitySignal | None, seed: int, policy_config: ArtifactRef): nonnegative time/energy budgets; freshness limits positive; all policies use identical declared inputs. Numeric values remain undecided.
LinkSample(stamp: ReplayStamp, available_at: ReplayStamp, state: Literal['up','degraded','lost'], latency_ticks: int | None, source: ArtifactRef): nonnegative delay or unavailable; no reading of live hardware.
QualitySignal(value: float, completed_at: ReplayStamp, available_at: ReplayStamp, generation_cost: CostEntry, source: ArtifactRef): actual recorded completed local step only, cost charged once via unique entry ID.
PlacementDecision(request_id: str, action: Literal['place','reject','abstain'], placement: Placement | None, reasons: tuple[str,...], input_digest: str): placement only for place; no hidden policy state. Feasibility order fixed by task class in policy config.
TraceEvent(event_id: str, stamp: ReplayStamp, available_at: ReplayStamp, sequence: int, kind: str, payload: LinkSample | StampedValue | RecordedResult): nonnegative stable sequence and immutable payload; tie order belongs to clock/event design.
FixedTrace(artifact: ArtifactRef, seed: int, model: ArtifactRef, clock: ReplayClock, events: tuple[TraceEvent,...]).
RecordedResult(request_id: str, completed_at: ReplayStamp | None, available_at: ReplayStamp | None, finding: FindingArtifact | None, cost: tuple[CostEntry,...]): missing completion stays None; completion and delivery are distinct.
ReplayBundle(artifact: ArtifactRef, tasks: tuple[TaskEnvelope,...], captures: tuple[CaptureStamp,...], trace: FixedTrace, results: tuple[RecordedResult,...], profiles: tuple[DeviceProfile,...], config: ArtifactRef): identity joins must be unique and total, no labels and no GPU regeneration.
CostEntry(entry_id: str, category: str, duration_ticks: int, energy_j: float | None, source: Literal['measured','declared','modelled'], source_ref: ArtifactRef): nonnegative values, each incurred category retained including discarded results, retries, queue and policy overhead.
RequestOutcome(request_id: str, submitted_at: ReplayStamp, deadline: ReplayStamp, completed_at: ReplayStamp | None, classification: Literal['on_time','late','not_completed'], costs: tuple[CostEntry,...], discarded_results: tuple[str,...]): all submissions appear exactly once; event history retained.
OutcomeLog(artifact: ArtifactRef, clock: ReplayClock, requests: tuple[RequestOutcome,...], input_refs: tuple[ArtifactRef,...], events: ArtifactRef).
ReplayAnalysisConfig(artifact: ArtifactRef, completion_boundary: str, equality_rule: str, observation_horizon: ReplayStamp): values fixed before run after Owner review, no default equality rule silently selected.
ReplayReport(provenance: EvaluationContext, submitted: int, on_time: int, late: int, not_completed: int, miss_rate: float | None, completed_percentiles_s: tuple[tuple[str,float | None],...], costs: ArtifactRef): counts nonnegative, sum equals submitted; miss=(late+not_completed)/submitted or N/A for zero submitted; completed percentiles conditional, no invented completion time.
MeasurementEvent(name: str, stamp: HostStamp).
MeasurementRecord(run_ref: ArtifactRef, host: DeviceInfo, state: Literal['cold','warm'], start: HostStamp, end: HostStamp | None, output_length: int | None, network_included: bool, warmup_count: int, repetition_index: int, tool_id: str, memory_mib: float | None, energy_j: float | None, outcome: Literal['completed','failed','timeout']): counts nonnegative; unsupported energy stays None. Clock/power mode retained in linked raw samples.
MeasurementReport(provenance: EvaluationContext, raw: ArtifactRef, boundary: str, percentiles_s: tuple[tuple[str,float | None],...], failures: int, cold_warm_separated: bool): required 50/95/99 percentiles come from 0022, not new targets; missing/failed intervals reported explicitly, never fabricated durations.
EvaluationPhase = Literal['training_development','calibration','frozen_test'].
SplitManifest(artifact: ArtifactRef, source: ArtifactRef, licence: ArtifactRef, split_id: str, phase: EvaluationPhase, groups: ArtifactRef, leakage_check: ArtifactRef): author original source only; unresolved groups excluded from heldout evaluation.
ReferenceFact(fact_id: str, image_id: str, class_id: str, region: Box | None, evidence: Literal['present','labelled_absent','unlabelled'], source: ArtifactRef): no absence inferred from omitted annotations.
ReferenceSet(manifest: SplitManifest, facts: tuple[ReferenceFact,...]): permitted only inside EVA offline path.
FreezePermit(config_sha256: str, split_refs: tuple[ArtifactRef,...], phase: EvaluationPhase, authorised: bool): approval metadata, not proof by itself; composition validates against retained approval.
EvaluationContext(run_record: ArtifactRef, inputs: tuple[ArtifactRef,...], protocol: ArtifactRef, reference_manifest: ArtifactRef | None, host_type: Literal['development-host'], phase: EvaluationPhase): used only offline; never forward reference_manifest to prediction components.
ScoreProtocol(artifact: ArtifactRef, family: str, parameters: tuple[tuple[str,float | str],...], matching_rule: str, aggregation_rule: str, unresolved: tuple[str,...]): any unresolved field blocks evaluation.
ScoreReport(provenance: EvaluationContext, submitted: int, accepted: int, accepted_scoreable: int, errors: int, unscoreable: int, malformed: int, failed: int, abstained: int, fact_counts: ArtifactRef, per_item: ArtifactRef, coverage: float | None, selective_risk: float | None): counts nonnegative; 0 <= errors <= accepted_scoreable <= accepted <= submitted. Unscoreable is a scoreability axis, not necessarily a mutually exclusive execution outcome. Coverage=accepted/submitted; selective risk=errors/accepted_scoreable; zero denominator => None/N/A.
RunSubmission(code_revision: str, config_hash: str, seed: int | None, seed_applicability: str, host_id: str, host_type: Literal['development-host'], device_id: str, model_id: str | None, precision: str | None, library_versions: tuple[tuple[str,str],...], raw_artifact: ArtifactRef, analysis_command: str, outcome: str): model-specific fields mandatory for inference, explicit not-applicable for non-inference; no fabricated model/seed. This is proposed record typing, not a requirement text edit.
RecordReceipt(record_ref: ArtifactRef, validated: bool).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDGE-ARC-TIME
TITLE: Clock mapping and event boundary design
STATUS: proposed
KIND: time contract
SOURCE: EDG-REQ-0007 0020 0021 0022 0024 0026 0032
STATEMENT: >>>
ReplayClock(clock_id: str, tick_period_s: Fraction, origin_id: str); ReplayStamp(clock_id: str, tick: int); CaptureStamp(image_id: str, original_clock_id: str, original_time_s: Fraction, mapping_ref: ArtifactRef, replay: ReplayStamp); HostStamp(clock_id: str, monotonic_ns: int). Integer ticks nonnegative; tick_period_s is positive rational and UNDECIDED by Owner (D-TIME-01). Nanoseconds in HostStamp describe the host counter representation, not a chosen replay resolution.
Mappings are explicit affine maps t_replay_s = a * t_source_s + b, with a positive rational (dimensionless), b rational seconds, source/target clock IDs and provenance. Maps are fixed before replay; no measured live drift correction during replay. Map all captures, trajectory samples, result availability and decisions onto the same clock. Require mapped_time / tick_period_s to be an exact integer; reject nonrepresentable inputs. Do not round timestamps silently. Owner selects resolution or revises the input design before execution.
Freshness comes from capture time in the fixed request/image bundle, not network delay alone: age_ticks = decision.tick - capture.replay.tick. Network trace determines delivery/availability, not a replacement capture timestamp. Future capture or cross-clock subtraction is rejected. Fresh iff age_ticks < result_freshness_ticks; equality is stale per 0024. A delivered stale result is discarded, retained and costed. Input signal age is checked separately using its own timestamp and declared freshness.
Event timestamps and availability timestamps are distinct. POL receives only entries with available_at <= current decision time and already-completed quality signals. Deterministic ordering is the predeclared tuple (tick, event_priority, sequence, event_id). Event priorities, same-tick arrival versus timeout ordering and deadline equality convention remain Owner decisions (D-TIME-02); absent policy blocks execution. No wall-clock ordering enters replay.
A timeout is a recorded event, not a completion. A late result can arrive after a timeout: record both events, charge its cost, and apply freshness independently. At the fixed observation horizon, classify every request once: completed at the declared end-to-end boundary -> on_time or late according to fixed deadline comparison; otherwise not_completed. A request timed out earlier but later completed within the observation horizon is not counted twice. Computational completion, delivery, usability and terminal action are distinct fields/events; Owner selects the request completion boundary and observation horizon (D-TIME-03).
No completion timestamp is written for not_completed requests. Completed-request percentiles exclude them and accompany not-completed/miss rates. These are replay outcomes, not actual inference timing claims.
Synthetic dimensional example (not run, no budget or threshold selected): let q=tick_period_s, capture=(C,10), trace sample=(C,12), delivery=(C,14), decision=(C,15). With identity source mapping, age=5*q seconds. For symbolic positive integer freshness F, fresh iff 5 < F; F=5 illustrates the existing equality-is-stale rule, not a selected operating value. With symbolic deadline D, completion at tick C_end is classified by the pending equality convention; if absent at horizon H, completed_at=None, regardless of a timeout event at D. The example uses no GPU or dataset and sets no clock resolution.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDGE-ARC-SCORE
TITLE: Offline matching families and undecided scoring parameters
STATUS: proposed
KIND: scoring design
SOURCE: EDG-REQ-0002 0013 0015 0016 0019 0030 0033
STATEMENT: >>>
No family or numeric threshold is selected here. All scoring and reference processing is confined to EVA's offline evaluation/calibration paths. Runtime predictions and abstentions are produced before reference lookup.
Family A: class-consistent spatial matching, using source-coordinate region overlap (box IoU, polygon overlap or another explicitly specified measure). Preconditions: reliable class and geometric references, fixed conversion of annotation polygons to scoring geometry, same source-image coordinates. One-to-one matching avoids duplicate credit. Candidate deterministic matching is maximum-weight bipartite assignment among eligible same-class pairs, with stable ID tie-breaking; greedy matching is an alternative with order sensitivity to disclose. Eligibility threshold and algorithm are Owner decisions. Box envelopes of polygons may overstate overlap; annotation incompleteness remains.
Family B: image-level class presence matching. Preconditions: reliable image-level positive/negative facts for the target classes. Ignores location accuracy and cannot by itself satisfy spatial finding evaluation under 0002/0018; useful as separately labelled auxiliary analysis. A missing annotation is not a negative image.
Family C: explicitly adjudicated finding/fact matching, using predeclared evidence-backed correspondence and scoreability. Preconditions: independent labelled facts, adjudication procedure and traceable decisions. It can handle partial labelling but adds adjudication work and must not be used to select favourable examples.
For all families: matched reliable positives support detections; unmatched reliable positives support missed-defect counts. An unmatched prediction is false only where reliable negative evidence refutes its class/region claim. No reliable negative evidence means undeterminable, not automatically false and not automatically correct. Unlabelled regions do not enter complete fabrication-rate claims. A valid no_finding can be refuted by a reliable relevant positive, supported by reliable absence evidence, or unscoreable when neither is sufficient.
Execution categories: valid findings/no_finding => accepted; abstain, invalid/malformed and execution failure => not accepted. Each submission remains in coverage denominator. Scoreability is a separate axis. ReferenceFact counts (present, labelled_absent, unlabelled, undeterminable) are retained per class. Partial scoreability and aggregation to an item error are explicit pending design choices: do not conflate fact-level errors with the accepted-item denominator of 0013. A definite supported error may establish item error; mixed supported/unknown facts require a predeclared aggregation policy, not arbitrary correct credit.
Parameters pending Owner decision: matching family, geometric representation, overlap measure and threshold, assignment/tie rule, duplicate treatment, per-item aggregation and partial-scoreability policy, no_finding support rule, abstention/confidence calibration method and thresholds, calibration objectives, policy feasibility/freshness/time/energy budgets and retries where used. No defaults or numeric choices are supplied.
Family/method choices and calibration procedure must be approved before test access. Any tunable numeric value in this scoring/threshold design is determined only on the isolated calibration split under that predeclared procedure; fitting/model/prompt selection remains training/development per 0019/0033. The test split is never used to choose a family, parameter, scorer or baseline; all hashes and unresolved decisions must be closed before its single evaluation. Describing a rule family now is not permission to calibrate or score.
<<<

