[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDGE-ARC-DECISIONS
TITLE: Owner decisions before S3 and later evaluation
STATUS: proposed
KIND: open decisions
SOURCE: EDG-REQ-0019 0021 0022 0024 0025 0033
STATEMENT: >>>
D-TIME-01: positive rational replay tick resolution and any allowed source-clock mapping constants. No numeric resolution selected.
D-TIME-02: deadline equality convention and same-tick event priorities (arrival/timeout/decision ordering). Freshness equality already fixed as stale by 0024 and is not reopened.
D-TIME-03: exact end-to-end request completion boundary, observation horizon and handling of events beyond horizon; not-completed remains without completion timestamp.
D-SCORE-01: select scoring family/geometry/matching algorithm and duplicate/tie handling.
D-SCORE-02: item-level aggregation and partial-scoreability/no_finding evidence policy.
D-CAL-01: calibration method/objective and overlap/abstention/confidence parameter values. All unresolved; determine numerical scoring parameters only on calibration under approved procedure, never test.
D-BUDGET-01: per-class freshness/time/energy budgets and fixed retry counts. No values selected. These are run design choices, not additions to edge.sdoc.
D-SCHEMA-01: approve candidate typed record evolution (kind-specific optional model/seed fields, provenance wrappers) for S3 implementation; no current code changed.
D-BASELINE-01: approve candidate architecture and whether/when to freeze requirements and architecture together. No tags created.
D-DATA-01: v2 is not read or scored here. Future independent v3 or format-only use requires a separate decision; no new dataset is authored here.
XC integration accountability is Owner as already decided; confirm in architecture review. No requirement text change is currently necessary to express these candidate contracts. If review identifies one, stop migration and present a separate change proposal.
This draft can be reviewed with explicit open choices; unresolved timing/scoring decisions prevent a claim of S3 execution readiness. No automatic migration on document export success.
<<<
